            "properties": {
                "0": {
                    "name": "block",
                    "value": "Makes an array longer by adding values before and after it along one axis. What the new values are depends on the mode: a constant, copies of the edge value, a mirror image of what is inside, or a wrap-around from the other end.\n\nUse it to bring arrays to a common length before stacking or comparing them, to give np.convolve or a smoothing filter something sensible to work on at the ends, to leave a margin round an image, or to zero-pad a window before np.fft.rfft for a finer-grained spectrum.\n\nSYNTAX:\nnp.pad <before: int> <after: int> <mode>\nDefaults: 1 before, 1 after, constant. A single number pads both sides.\n\nEXAMPLES:\nnp.pad 2\nnp.pad 0 10\nnp.pad 3 edge\n\nINPUTS and PARAMETERS:\n\nin:\nThe array (a list is turned into one). Every input is padded and sent.\n\nbefore (int box, also an inlet):\nHow many values to add before the start.\n\nafter (int box, also an inlet):\nHow many values to add after the end.\n\nvalue (float box, also an inlet):\nWhat the new values are in constant mode.\n\naxis (int box, also an inlet):\nWhich way to pad: -1 (the default) along each row, 0 above and below the columns.\n\nmode:\nAn option, under the node:\nconstant   the value, 0 unless set\nedge       copies of the first or last value\nreflect    a mirror image, not repeating the edge value (3 2 | 1 2 3 | 2 1)\nsymmetric  a mirror image that does repeat it (2 1 | 1 2 3 | 3 2)\nwrap       continue from the other end, as if the array repeated\n\nOUTPUTS:\n\npadded:\nThe longer array.\n\nREADING THE DEMO:\n1 2 3 padded by 2 on each side three ways: with zeros, 0 0 1 2 3 0 0; with the edge values, 1 1 1 2 3 3 3; and wrapped round, 2 3 1 2 3 1 2. A metro re-sends the array five times a second.\n\nRELATED:\nnp.concatenate joins two arrays end to end. np.tile repeats a whole array. np.crop and np.[] go the other way, cutting the edges off.",
                    "value_type": "str"
                },
                "1": {
                    "name": "lock",
                    "value": true,
                    "value_type": "bool"
                },
                "2": {
                    "name": "width",
                    "value": 760,
                    "value_type": "int"
                },
                "3": {
                    "name": "height",
